# Fixed defect 2431, 2026-11-10, lane b30-pkg, the whole message: `json`, a
# folder of the author's own, writes `use core/strconv`, `core` an entry of
# its own catalogue whose folder holds `strconv.hero`, and `json` has no
# `core/strconv.hero`.
#
# The repair writing `use <core>/strconv` is `certain` (panel 235's R18):
# nothing on the package's own side answers that path, the entry's tree holds
# the module, and the file stands in a folder the author edits, so `check
# <directory> --apply --in-place` writes it and the program checks clean,
# measured. Its neighbour in a placed tree is a `guess`
# (`fixedbugs-2431-a-repair-in-a-placed-packages-tree-is-a-guess`).
use <json>/parse

function main()
    print(parse.word())
